note How a call site becomes an edge in the call graph. The two backends give two different things: tree-sitter gives raw (name, qualifier) strings, a language server gives the (file, line) of the callee's definition. link turns both into callee/caller lists, rebuilding every edge from scratch each time. Server targets are exact; tree-sitter targets go through resolve, a qualifier-aware but type-free heuristic whose rules are the ones written on resolve itself. This is why the map's xrefs are trustworthy with rust-analyzer on PATH and approximate without it.

